  "verbalization": "Gerontoisoflavone A appears to interact with Serine/threonine-protein kinase MARK2 through a series of molecular pathways involving K-252a, a known target of Gerontoisoflavone A. The evidence suggests that Gerontoisoflavone A acts as a target of K-252a, which in turn targets MARK2. This indicates a potential regulatory relationship where Gerontoisoflavone A may modulate the activity of MARK2 through K-252a. The overlapping targets of K-252a across different paths suggest a possible mechanism of action involving kinase signaling pathways, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The consistent presence of K-252a as a mediator in multiple pathways supports the hypothesis that Gerontoisoflavone A influences MARK2 through this intermediate, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction.",
